// Races and positions that exist in both BBL and TP source data under
// slightly different names, pre-registered here (before the BBL/TP
// importers run) so each importer's upsert matches this single record
// instead of creating a duplicate.
//
// Races: BBL names its team-page race "<Race> Team"/"<Race> Teams"; TP
// names the same race just "<Race>". Paired below by stripping that suffix.
// A race whose BBL and TP names already matched verbatim (e.g. every
// "College of X", and "Slann") merged automatically via the shared "Name"
// external id and needs no entry here.
//
// Positions: both BBL and TP key a position by "<raceName>: <positionName>"
// under the "Name" external id (see NameExternalIdService.forPosition and
// TpPositionsImportService/BblPositionsImportService). A position whose BBL
// and TP position name already match verbatim merges automatically via that
// shared "Name" id and needs no entry here, the same as the race case above.
// Only positions whose BBL and TP position name genuinely differs are listed
// below: each registers both source systems' raw ids (BBL's
// "<typId>-<raceBblId>" and TP's numeric position id) plus TP's own "Name" id
// (its own spelling) so a later TP upsert's automatically-attached id lands on
// this same row rather than looking new. Pairs were found two ways: (1)
// programmatically, same race (per the pairing above) and the same position
// name once case, plural (-s/-es/-ies, including irregular ones like
// -men/-man) and punctuation differences are normalized away; (2) by a
// manual race-by-race review recognizing same-role renames a string match
// can't catch (e.g. "DB Big Un Blocker" / "Big Un Blocker", "Elven Blitzers"
// / "Elf Blitzer", "Anointed Blitzer" / "Tomb Kings Blitzer"). Wording that
// differs by more than a recognizable rename (e.g. Amazon's BBL "Piranha
// Warrior Catcher" vs TP "Piranha Warrior Blitzer" -- looks like a genuine
// roster reshuffle between rule editions, not a naming variant -- or the
// many BB2020-only/CRP-only positions with no counterpart at all, was left
// out rather than guessed at, since a wrong guess would silently conflate
// two different roster slots.
{
  externalSystems: [
    { name: 'tloeg.bbleague.se', category: 'imported_data_source' },
    { name: 'tourplay.net', category: 'imported_data_source' },
    { name: 'Name', category: 'bookkeeping' },
  ],
